  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore Urban Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952. There was no contest; all the retiring members except Mr. John Patterson were re-nominated and Mr. R. N. Jamison filled the vacant seat (Dromore Leader, 10 May 1952, p. 3). Mr. R. N. Jamison, proposed by Mr. S. J. Duffy and seconded by Mr. Jas. Shannon, filled the seat vacated by Mr. John Patterson. Returned unopposed."
